  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Clinique Vétérinaire de la Croix Rouge, 1238 route de Grasse in Antibes, is run by two partner vets, Dr Philippe Boudeville and Dr Jean-François Buisse, with a veterinary assistant. According to its website, the team receives animals in two linked sites, one in the heart of Juan-les-Pins near the Pinède, the other in the Croix Rouge district of Antibes.</p>
      <p>Dr Boudeville holds advanced certificates in veterinary dermatology and ophthalmology and is approved for canine and feline insemination; Dr Buisse is mainly involved in bone and joint, neurological and skin surgery. The clinic also provides reproduction follow-up for individuals and breeders.</p>
      <p>As for facilities, the website cites a waiting room, a consultation room, an equipped surgery room, an X-ray area and cages for hospitalising dogs and cats. A dog and cat grooming salon is next door; free private car parks are available.</p>

      <h2>Opening hours</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Monday to Friday: 8:30am-12:00pm and 2:00pm-7:00pm.</li>
        <li>Saturday: 8:30am-12:00pm.</li>
        <li>Sunday: closed.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Emergencies</h2>
      <p>The clinic's website states that outside opening hours emergencies are handled at the clinic 24/7 with a simple phone call to 04 93 74 87 07.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: keep this number saved in your phone if you're staying around Antibes, and call before heading over.</div>

      <h2>Practical</h2>
      <p>The clinic speaks French and English, accepts payment plans and pet insurance (clinic website). It also offers an online e-health record.</p>
